WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Type II is the bread and butter of residential HVAC. This is what you'll use
every day.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Type II covers high-pressure systems — the most common HVAC equipment including
residential AC, commercial rooftop units, and heat pumps. These systems use
refrigerants like R-410A, R-22, and R-134a that operate above atmospheric

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
High-Pressure System: System operating above atmospheric pressure on both sides.
Includes most residential and commercial AC.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Type II is the most important certification
for residential and commercial HVAC technicians.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Most of your career will involve Type II systems. And —
R-410A operates at significantly higher pressures than R-22

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
What recovery level do you need on a system under 200 pounds using post-1993
equipment? Know that cold.

